hips its own reassembly and `dao.stream.udp` is left untouched.\n   573\t  The slice report says which was taken and why.\n   574\t- Real covered-index nodes are measured against `max-message-bytes`.\n   575\t- JVM↔Node and JVM↔Dart pass the same wire tests.\n   576\t- `dao.jing.cbor.md` (Remote and DHT) is updated to this wire.\n   577\t- `dao.jing`'s Base64 functions are repointed onto `dao.stream.base64`.\n   578\t\n   579\t**S4 — hardening, lookup repair, storage bound.** Depends on S3. The keyed\n   580\t`cookie-for` replacing the S2 stand-in, the chunk path under the gate, and\n   581\tevery bound. Acceptance:\n   582\t- A cookie cannot be computed without the secret; the S2 stand-in is gone.\n   583\t- A spoofed source elicits at most one reply, never larger than the datagram\n   584\t  it sent, and silence when the reply would be larger; it allocates nothing.\n   585\t  Tested across datagram sizes from 1 byte to the budget, chunks included.\n   586\t- A reply from an unexpected source is ignored; a claimed address never\n   587\t  enters the table.\n   588\t- A live next-nearest peer is tried after dead peers, and dead peers leave\n   589\t  the table.\n   590\t- Inbound storage at its bound refuses explicitly.\n   591\t- `publish?` false neither originates nor serves.\n   592\t- Non-loopback exposure is permitted only after this slice.\n   593\t\n   594\t**S5 — REPL integration.** Depends on S4 and on the durable-store epic (spec,\n   595\tHEAD, lock, recovery). Acceptance:\n   596\t- Default `mem`; `dht:<dir>` is explicit; with no peers it is solo and opens\n   597\t  no socket.\n   598\t- Publishing requires its own flag, separate from peers, and the REPL states\n   599\t  what will be shared before it shares.\n   600\t- The REPL shows per publication whether it is acknowledged (sent to N\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
